WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.310
In 1994, new HIV infections peaked.

2
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:07.905
Since then, they have
fallen by 65 per cent.

3
00:00:07.955 --> 00:00:12.850
AIDS-related deaths are
down 73 per cent since 2004.

4
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:19.130
Yet in 2025, 41.0 million
people were living with HIV.

5
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:21.030
So what drove the fall?

6
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:22.070
Condoms alone?

7
00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.470
A weaker virus?

8
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.170
And why are some groups still left behind?

9
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:29.290
In this mission, you'll separate
prevention from treatment,

10
00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:34.310
and see what a trial
of 1,763 couples found.

11
00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.810
Then you'll match strategy
to the means of infection,

12
00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:40.330
for cholera, malaria and HIV.

13
00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:44.410
Your mission: explain what drove
the fall in new HIV infections,

14
00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.840
and why some groups are left behind.
